MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=874
We have the decay:  
π⁺ → μ⁺ + ν  
π⁺ at rest, so initial momentum = 0.  
Let m_π = 139.6 MeV/c², m_μ = 105.7 MeV/c², neutrino mass ≈ 0.

Energy conservation:  
m_π c² = E_μ + E_ν  
Momentum conservation:  
p_μ = p_ν (magnitudes equal, opposite directions).

For muon: E_μ² = (p c)² + (m_μ c²)²  
For neutrino: E_ν = p c (since massless).

Let p be magnitude of momentum (in units where c=1).  
Then:  
E_μ = √(p² + m_μ²)  
E_ν = p  
m_π = √(p² + m_μ²) + p

Solve for p:  
m_π - p = √(p² + m_μ²)  
Square:  
(m_π - p)² = p² + m_μ²  
m_π² - 2 m_π p + p² = p² + m_μ²  
m_π² - 2 m_π p = m_μ²  
2 m_π p = m_π² - m_μ²  
p = (m_π² - m_μ²) / (2 m_π)

Plug numbers:  
m_π² = (139.6)² = 19488.16  
m_μ² = (105.7)² = 11172.49  
Difference = 19488.16 - 11172.49 = 8315.67  
Divide by 2 m_π = 279.2 →
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

