QUESTION_PROMPT_END
MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=914
We need the threshold energy for pair production:  
A high-energy photon (energy \(E_\gamma\)) collides with a CMB photon (energy \(\epsilon \sim 10^{-3}\) eV).  
The reaction \(\gamma + \gamma \to e^+ + e^-\) requires center-of-mass energy \(\ge 2 m_e c^2\).  
For head-on collision, the invariant energy is \(\sqrt{4 E_\gamma \epsilon}\) (since \(E_\gamma \gg \epsilon\)).  
Threshold condition:  
\[
\sqrt{4 E_\gamma \epsilon} \ge 2 m_e c^2
\]  
\[
4 E_\gamma \epsilon \ge 4 m_e^2 c^4
\]  
\[
E_\gamma \ge \frac{m_e^2 c^4}{\epsilon}
\]  
With \(m_e c^2 = 0.511 \text{ MeV} = 5.11 \times 10^5 \text{ eV}\), and \(\epsilon = 10^{-3} \text{ eV}\):  
\[
E_\gamma \ge \frac{(5.11\times 10^5)^2}{10^{-3}} \text{ eV} = \frac{2.61\times 10^{11}}{10^{-3}} \text{ eV} = 2.61\times 10^{14} \text{ eV}
\]  
Convert to GeV: \(2.61\times 10^{14} \text{ eV} = 2.61\times 10^5 \text{ GeV}\).  
That matches choice B.

Answer: B
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

